From: Claude <claude@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:47:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] feat(store): validate on every load, back up unreadable
 data, show a recovery banner

- persist.merge runs the zod-validated migrate() on every hydration (zustand only calls
  persist.migrate when the version differs, so partial settings used to slip through)
- Corrupt JSON / non-backup / newer-version data is copied to localStorage key alcc:v1:backup
  before anything can overwrite it; the app falls back to defaults instead of failing silently
- Failed localStorage writes are logged instead of throwing into the UI
- hydrateStore() replaces the inline rehydrate in AppShell; Loading can no longer hang on errors
- Dismissible banner with 'Download original data' when data was skipped, repaired or reset
- Tests for hydration (incl. mutation-checked) and store actions
